WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:06.240
The fabric of our world is littered with doorways&nbsp;
if you know where to look for them. Tears,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:13.440
portals, anomalies, all leading to places and&nbsp;
planes beyond human imagining and understanding,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:18.640
and SCP-2317, otherwise known&nbsp;
as A Door to Another World,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:24.160
certainly fits that description. Contained and&nbsp;
kept at all times under the watch of armed guards,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:30.080
SCP-2317 appears to be a simple and&nbsp;
unsuspecting wooden door in its frame.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:35.120
It hardly looks like it requires such extreme&nbsp;
round-the-clock security or needs a strange,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:41.120
secretive ritual that the Foundation performs,&nbsp;
presumably to keep the door closed. But,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:46.080
of course, sometimes the most interesting thing&nbsp;
about a closed doorway isn’t where it leads,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:51.840
it’s what it keeps out.
Even by the Foundation’s already-high standards,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:57.440
the requirements and regulations for&nbsp;
personnel who are assigned to SCP-2317&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.440 --> 00:01:02.800
seem oddly specific. Psychological testing is&nbsp;
standard practice for to work for the Foundation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:08.480
but an additional hurdle that anyone has to clear&nbsp;
before even getting to glimpse at this unassuming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:13.520
wooden door is having a score of at least&nbsp;
seventy-two on the Milgram Obedience Examination.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.480 --> 00:01:19.120
It is also mandatory that personnel assigned&nbsp;
to maintaining it are both unmarried, with no&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:24.960
children or next-of-kin, as well as an unwavering,&nbsp;
unquestioning loyalty to the Foundation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:31.520
pure devotion to its code and objectives.&nbsp;
These may seem like strange requirements,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:39.200
after all, SCP-2317 is just a door…isn’t it?
Perhaps there’s a reason that the Foundation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:45.760
keeps so much of the information about SCP-2317&nbsp;
buried deep under layers upon layers of security,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.760 --> 00:01:51.680
with only the Overseer Council privy to the&nbsp;
full details of its strange nature. Knowledge,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:57.760
as they say, is power - but maybe knowing too&nbsp;
much about whatever is behind that door can prove&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.760 --> 00:02:05.520
deadly. Still, if SCP-2317 is a Door to Another&nbsp;
World, an alternate dimension or parallel reality,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:11.040
it must be safe enough to visit. After all, the&nbsp;
Foundation has been sending personnel in there on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.040 --> 00:02:18.400
a regular basis. Daily, in fact. According to the&nbsp;
O5 Council, this is done as part of a procedure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:24.560
to maintain Active Containment of…something&nbsp;
lurking beyond that old wooden doorframe.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:28.800
But what could possibly warrant such&nbsp;
constant maintenance and surveillance?&nbsp;

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:35.200
In accordance with the Foundation’s guidelines,&nbsp;
all staff are required to rotate out of observing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:41.120
SCP-2317 after every two months and spend the&nbsp;
following third month in full psychological&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:45.280
counselling before they are permitted to&nbsp;
return to the containment unit housing the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.280 --> 00:02:50.400
Door to Another World. It was after one of&nbsp;
these month-long periods of evaluation that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:55.840
a Foundation guard was informed that his security&nbsp;
clearance had been raised to Level 3 and that he’d&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.840 --> 00:03:01.040
been selected for the duty of carrying out&nbsp;
220-Calabasas. He knew the name instantly;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:06.720
this was the title given to the daily containment&nbsp;
procedure that absolutely had to be carried out.&nbsp;

00:03:07.840 --> 00:03:12.160
The guard didn’t question these orders, after&nbsp;
all, he’d been selected precisely because of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.160 --> 00:03:18.000
his loyalty to the Foundation. He did make one&nbsp;
request to his commanding officer, however:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:21.520
he wanted to know what had happened to the&nbsp;
last guard that had performed the procedure.&nbsp;

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:26.640
“Didn’t make it out of psychological&nbsp;
evaluation,” the officer replied.&nbsp;

00:03:27.760 --> 00:03:33.040
Not letting this affect his dedication, the guard&nbsp;
was told to prepare for Procedure 220-Calabasas.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:38.800
Along with a fellow member of Foundation security&nbsp;
personnel, the guard was instructed to gather&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:44.160
everything on a strange list. The first was&nbsp;
a pre-selected member of Class-D Personnel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.720 --> 00:03:50.240
specifically a convicted murderer. Class-D&nbsp;
refers to ‘Disposable Class’ personnel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.240 --> 00:03:55.520
expendable individuals recruited by the&nbsp;
Foundation for the sole purpose of testing SCPs.&nbsp;

00:03:56.560 --> 00:04:01.360
Class-Ds were usually prison inmates&nbsp;
repurposed for SCP testing, and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.360 --> 00:04:07.280
one chosen for 220-Calabasas was no exception,&nbsp;
serving multiple life sentences for murders,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:10.960
or at least that was what the guard&nbsp;
had been told. A Foundation personnel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.960 --> 00:04:15.360
member instructed him to refer to the Class-D&nbsp;
solely as the ‘assistant’ from that point on.&nbsp;

00:04:16.240 --> 00:04:21.440
Next, the guard collected a live chicken, an&nbsp;
obsidian-edged knife, a silver aspergillum&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.440 --> 00:04:26.880
and aspersorium, to be filled with 500ccs of&nbsp;
Holy Water that had been blessed by a priest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.880 --> 00:04:33.600
of the Abrahamic faith, and finally a one-kiloton&nbsp;
nuclear device, which, according to instructions,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:38.240
was to only be detonated in the unlikely&nbsp;
event of a catastrophic containment failure.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.240 --> 00:04:43.680
In other words, the last resort.
After following his instructions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.680 --> 00:04:48.400
to the letter and without question, the guard&nbsp;
and his colleague were briefed. The Foundation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.400 --> 00:04:51.920
personnel member informed them that he’d be&nbsp;
joining and leading them in the procedure.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:57.280
The staff member also specified that henceforth&nbsp;
he be referred to as the ‘celebrant’ until the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.280 --> 00:05:03.600
completion of 220-Calabasas. The guard was acutely&nbsp;
aware of how specific these instructions were,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.600 --> 00:05:08.000
but trusted in the Foundation, knowing that&nbsp;
if they wanted this procedure performed a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:12.480
certain way, then it was in everyones’ best&nbsp;
interest to carry out the orders to the letter.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.120 --> 00:05:18.960
But what the celebrant then went on to explain,&nbsp;
raised far more questions about SCP-2317&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.600 --> 00:05:27.120
and the nature of Procedure 220-Calabasas. The&nbsp;
Class-D joining them, wasn’t actually a Class-D.&nbsp;

00:05:28.080 --> 00:05:32.640
The assistant, as they were now referred to,&nbsp;
was in reality another Foundation staff member,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.200 --> 00:05:37.840
with a Level 4 security clearance,&nbsp;
specifically tailored to SCP-2317.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.040 --> 00:05:45.600
Every member of staff entering through SCP-2317&nbsp;
and taking an active role in 220-Calabasas needed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.600 --> 00:05:50.400
to be informed that this assistant was not to be&nbsp;
harmed or treated as a member of Disposable Class.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.360 --> 00:05:55.680
Fighting back the nagging question of why&nbsp;
the Foundation would employ this subterfuge,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.240 --> 00:06:00.800
the guard, along with his fellow security&nbsp;
officer, the celebrant and assistant,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.800 --> 00:06:04.320
prepared for their departure through&nbsp;
the Door to Another World at solar noon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.960 --> 00:06:11.920
when the sun was highest over SCP-2317.&nbsp;
Solar noon, chickens and holy water,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.800 --> 00:06:16.240
this all seemed like an oddly-occult&nbsp;
combination for the Foundation.&nbsp;

00:06:17.200 --> 00:06:22.480
As they entered the old wooden door, beyond lay a&nbsp;
barren salt plane, stretching out for kilometers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.480 --> 00:06:28.240
in every direction. This alternate dimension,&nbsp;
according to the briefing, was designated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:28.240 --> 00:06:34.000
SCP-2317-Prime. The guard immediately noticed&nbsp;
a ring of seven pillars directly ahead&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:38.720
of the group as they entered, each of them&nbsp;
bearing intricately-detailed engravings&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.720 --> 00:06:45.440
unlike anything from any era of ancient history.
Procedure 220-Calabasas was carried out quickly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.440 --> 00:06:50.560
but carefully, the guard watching as the celebrant&nbsp;
and assistant were careful not to miss a step.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:51.680 --> 00:06:54.960
First, the celebrant scattered Holy Water&nbsp;
into the center of the pillars with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.960 --> 00:07:00.240
aspergillum and aspersorium, looking down&nbsp;
at his feet and keeping a steady pace as he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.240 --> 00:07:05.440
stepped counter-clockwise around them. The guard&nbsp;
watched intently as the celebrant completed his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.440 --> 00:07:10.640
circuit around the pillars and turned to the&nbsp;
assistant, anointing his head with Holy Water.&nbsp;

00:07:11.440 --> 00:07:18.160
“Seven Seals, Seven Rings, Seven Thrones&nbsp;
for the Scarlet King,” he said aloud.&nbsp;

00:07:19.120 --> 00:07:23.120
The assistant, with the obsidian blade in&nbsp;
his hand, took the chicken and dispatched it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:23.120 --> 00:07:28.880
in sacrifice, letting its blood mix with the&nbsp;
Holy Water. He then repeated the celebrant’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:28.880 --> 00:07:32.800
circuit in the opposite direction, before&nbsp;
stepping into the center of the stone pillars.&nbsp;

00:07:33.920 --> 00:07:40.160
“Blood for the Old Gods, Water for the New King,”&nbsp;
the assistant recited, pouring the remaining mix&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:40.160 --> 00:07:44.160
of blood and Holy Water over a patch of&nbsp;
salt in the middle of the seven pillars.&nbsp;

00:07:45.280 --> 00:07:50.160
Even though he knew it wasn’t his place to&nbsp;
question the Foundation, as the 220-Calabasas&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:50.160 --> 00:07:54.960
procedure took place, the guard couldn’t&nbsp;
help but wonder what all this was for.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:55.760 --> 00:08:02.400
It seemed so…ritualistic, like something&nbsp;
deeply religious or even magical. He’d never&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.400 --> 00:08:06.320
bought into all that occult mumbo-jumbo,&nbsp;
even while working for the Foundation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:06.880 --> 00:08:12.480
but he had learned not to question anything, even&nbsp;
the strangest and most inexplicable of sights.&nbsp;

00:08:13.760 --> 00:08:18.960
Little did he know that beneath his feet,&nbsp;
was an ancient and unknowable horror.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:19.600 --> 00:08:25.600
A beast, chained and lying in wait. Contained&nbsp;
in a chamber directly underneath the pillars,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:25.600 --> 00:08:31.360
sat an impossibly-large creature. Humanoid&nbsp;
and obese, its body covered entirely in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:31.360 --> 00:08:37.200
scales thicker than armour plating. Branch-like&nbsp;
horns protruded from its jawless head, pointing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:37.200 --> 00:08:43.280
up to chains that hung from the seven pillars&nbsp;
above, each one hooked into the entity’s back.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.240 --> 00:08:49.440
All but one of the chains was broken, a&nbsp;
final, withering shackle keeping the Devourer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:49.440 --> 00:08:56.160
of Worlds in its underground prison.
Ever since 1894 BCE, when Erikeshan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.160 --> 00:09:01.040
mystics imprisoned it, the Devourer has been&nbsp;
waiting patiently for its inevitable freedom.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.680 --> 00:09:06.720
It knows, as well as the Foundation, that nothing&nbsp;
can be done to prevent the final chain from one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:06.720 --> 00:09:13.440
day breaking. Even Procedure 220-Calabasas won’t&nbsp;
keep the creature contained, it’s nothing more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:13.440 --> 00:09:20.000
than a smokescreen, an act, designed to create&nbsp;
an illusion of active containment and maintain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:27.040
Foundation morale until a permanent solution&nbsp;
can be devised to keep SCP-2317 imprisoned.&nbsp;

00:09:28.240 --> 00:09:33.280
Of course, if the guard had known this, it would&nbsp;
have also explained the need for a one-kiloton&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:33.280 --> 00:09:39.440
nuclear device as part of this staged ritual.&nbsp;
Procedure 220-Calabasas has all the components&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:39.440 --> 00:09:44.640
to trick everyone below the O5 Council,&nbsp;
emulating religious and occult rituals,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:44.640 --> 00:09:48.160
the increased level of security&nbsp;
surrounding the procedure and its purpose,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:49.040 --> 00:09:55.360
and telling staff that any failure to correctly,&nbsp;
and completely, perform the 220-Calabasas&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:55.360 --> 00:10:02.320
procedure will result in an XK-Class End of the&nbsp;
World Scenario. All these elements work together&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:02.320 --> 00:10:08.400
to conceal the truth: that one day, the Devourer&nbsp;
will escape and lay waste to our dimension.&nbsp;

00:10:09.920 --> 00:10:16.400
Knowledge is power, and maybe knowing too&nbsp;
much truly is deadly. Perhaps if the guard&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:16.400 --> 00:10:21.120
had learned any of this, he’d have understood why&nbsp;
his predecessor never made it out of psychological&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:21.120 --> 00:10:27.040
evaluation. Maybe if he had questioned the purpose&nbsp;
of Procedure 220-Calabasas, he'd have learned the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:27.040 --> 00:10:35.280
true nature of SCP-2317, and what that doorway&nbsp;
kept out. But he was loyal to the Foundation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.280 --> 00:10:40.320
through and through. As the team finished&nbsp;
performing 220-Calabasas and returned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:40.320 --> 00:10:45.840
though the wooden door, the guard took one last&nbsp;
glance over his shoulder at the vast salt plane.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:46.480 --> 00:10:52.720
The entire dimension was calm, silent,&nbsp;
but not peaceful: it was patient.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:53.440 --> 00:10:58.400
The entity had waited centuries for its time,&nbsp;
and now all it would take was the breaking of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:58.400 --> 00:11:04.800
the seventh and final chain. One day.
The door was closed behind the guard&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:04.800 --> 00:11:10.080
as he, the celebrant, the assistant and his&nbsp;
fellow security officer stepped back through,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:11.200 --> 00:11:16.480
their work done and, as far as they knew,&nbsp;
preventing catastrophe for another day.&nbsp;

00:11:17.600 --> 00:11:22.560
Only the Foundation higher-ups, the Overseer&nbsp;
Council, are aware of the true danger posed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:22.560 --> 00:11:29.680
by SCP-2317 and its sole inhabitant. Current&nbsp;
predictions are that at some point within the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:29.680 --> 00:11:35.840
next thirty years, the Devourer of Worlds will&nbsp;
be freed. Any and all attempts to repair or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:35.840 --> 00:11:42.480
recreate the chains holding it in place have so&nbsp;
far failed. As such, the O5 Council has elected&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:42.480 --> 00:11:48.720
to continue providing Foundation personnel with&nbsp;
the ignorant hope that Procedure 220-Calabasas&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:48.720 --> 00:11:55.040
is an effective strategy for containment.
As we’ve said, sometimes the most interesting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:55.040 --> 00:11:59.040
thing about a closed door isn’t where&nbsp;
it leads, it’s what it keeps out.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:59.840 --> 00:12:06.800
In the case of SCP-2317, the unassuming wooden&nbsp;
door holds at bay an ancient creature of untold&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:06.800 --> 00:12:13.760
power, that will one day break free and wreak&nbsp;
havoc in our dimension. Nothing the Foundation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:13.760 --> 00:12:19.920
does can prevent it, or keep it contained behind&nbsp;
the Door to Another World, and only the Overseer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:19.920 --> 00:12:26.480
Council knows that any and all efforts to&nbsp;
do so are futile. With all that in mind,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:26.480 --> 00:12:34.240
we can only hope that the doorway of SCP-2317&nbsp;
stays closed, at least for a little while longer.&nbsp;

00:12:35.520 --> 00:12:42.480
Now go check out “SCP – 3008 – Trapped In&nbsp;
Ikea” and “SCP – 106 – The Old Man Explained”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:43.200 --> 00:12:49.760
for more peeks behind the door of our reality&nbsp;
into the world of the frightening and strange.

